	Technical Stack Recommendation for 2026
The selection of a technical stack for a retail OS must prioritize runtime safety, production stability, and the ability to handle high-concurrency event streams while maintaining transactional integrity.9 The recommended stack for HelloKhata balances the rapid development cycle of modern JavaScript frameworks with the robustness of enterprise-grade backend services.
Frontend and Client-Side Infrastructure
The frontend is engineered using Next.js 16, leveraging the App Router to enforce a server-first architecture.3 This choice is driven by the framework's promotion of Turbopack as the default bundler, which significantly reduces development startup times and production build cycles.3 The use of React 19.2 is critical for its advanced UI features, specifically the <Activity /> component and useEffectEvent hook.3
The <Activity /> component allows the AI Drawer to remain mounted in the background without incurring the performance cost of continuous rendering, preserving state when the user switches between the POS interface and the AI analytics view.14 This is paired with Tailwind CSS for styling, utilizing an "Elite Dark" design system with an Emerald primary color (#00C896) to reduce visual fatigue for shopkeepers during extended periods of use.1
AI and Intelligence Layer
The intelligence layer is powered by the z-ai-web-dev-sdk, which provides a structured framework for managing multi-turn conversations and complex context requirements.16 For local language processing, the system utilizes the native Web Speech API for low-latency Speech-to-Text (STT) and Text-to-Speech (TTS).1 While standard models like Whisper or GPT-4o are used for general reasoning, the system architecture allows for the integration of fine-tuned local models like Ekush LLM to better handle Bangladeshi regional dialects and retail slang.2
Backend and Persistence Layer
The backend architecture follows a microservices pattern, ideally using Node.js (NestJS) for its non-blocking architecture and seamless integration with the TypeScript-first frontend.18 For data persistence, PostgreSQL is the primary choice due to its strong ACID compliance and support for complex relational queries essential for financial ledgers.18 To support the AI Engine's retrieval needs, a vector database such as Pinecone or the pgvector extension is recommended for managing semantic embeddings of the shop's inventory and FAQ datasets.18


